Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/mdp5: allow the last mixer stage in atomic check

Mixer stage IDs start at one (STAGE_BASE), with zero meaning unused.
The last assigned stage is cnt + start - 1. Reject it only when it exceeds
the configured stage count, not when it equals that count. The cursor path
already assigns nb_stages itself, and STAGE_MAX includes stage ID eight.

On MSM8226 nb_stages is two. The old comparison rejects a fullscreen base
plus a foreground on STAGE0, as well as a single non-fullscreen plane
which needs border color on the base stage. Both fail TEST_ONLY with
EINVAL before any hardware programming. Do not change the hardware stage
count or permit a third stage on this SoC.

Device validation and limitations: docs/GRAPHICS-BOTTLENECK.md.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_crtc.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_crtc.c
@@ -765,9 +765,10 @@ static int mdp5_crtc_atomic_check(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 	start = get_start_stage(crtc, crtc_state, &pstates[0].state->base);
 
 	/* verify that there are not too many planes attached to crtc
-	 * and that we don't have conflicting mixer stages:
+	 * and that we don't have conflicting mixer stages. Stage IDs start
+	 * at STAGE_BASE (1), so nb_stages itself is a valid last stage.
 	 */
-	if ((cnt + start - 1) >= hw_cfg->lm.nb_stages) {
+	if ((cnt + start - 1) > hw_cfg->lm.nb_stages) {
 		DRM_DEV_ERROR(dev->dev, "too many planes! cnt=%d, start stage=%d\n",
 			cnt, start);
 		return -EINVAL;
